{'symbol': 'APH', 'date': '2019-10-23 22:30:00', 'title': 'Amphenol Corporation Provides Earnings Guidance for the Fourth Quarter of 2019; Revises Earnings Guidance for the Full Year of 2019', 'text': 'Amphenol Corporation provided earnings guidance for the fourth quarter and revised earnings guidance for the full year of 2019. For the fourth quarter, the company expects sales to be in the range of $1.960 billion to $2.000 billion. Diluted EPS expected to be in the range of $0.89 to $0.91.  For the full year 2019, The company expects sales in the range of $8.035 billion to $8.075 billion, a decrease of 2% over 2018. This compares to the prior full-year 2019 guidance for sales in the range of $7.920 billion to $8.000 billion. Diluted EPS expected to be in the range of $3.61 to $3.63.'}
{'symbol': 'ANSS', 'date': '2019-10-23 22:30:00', 'title': 'ASE Group Significantly Advances Semiconductor Packaging Development with ANSYS Customization Toolkit Solution', 'text': "ASE Group (ASE) engineers have drastically improved their integrated circuit (IC) semiconductor packaging and development process to create microchips by ANSYS. Developing an ANSYS Customization Toolkit (ACT) solution, engineers create more accurate models, enhance structural reliability and slash design time to enable customers to receive products faster than ever. As IC manufacturing processes become more complex, companies have shifted focus to product design and dedicating less development time to simulation. As a result, engineers cannot capture reliability problems, optimum designs cannot be created and product reliability becomes compromised, requiring vast redesign expenses. To improve the IC packaging and development process, engineers must quickly create models that span countless scenarios to identify design problems and boost product performance. Leveraging extensive process experience and best practices, ASE has developed an ANSYS ACT workflow. This streamlined sub-modeling automation solution enhances the IC packaging and development process. ASE's ANSYS ACT extension drastically reduces human error by converting complex manual analyses into an automatic search process to identify critical reliability issues such as cracking and interface delamination. This enables ASE engineers to swiftly create highly precise models, rapidly determine the optimal solution, identify problematic parts and reduce overall development time by 30%."}
{'symbol': 'ANTM', 'date': '2019-10-23 12:30:00', 'title': 'Anthem CEO Says "Very Positive" About Overall Medicaid Environment Going Forward', 'text': 'ANTHEM SAYS ON TRACK TO HAVE ALL MEMBERS MIGRATE TO INGENIORX PLATFORM BY JAN 1, 2020 - CONF. CALL.ANTHEM SAYS UNFAVORABLE TRENDS IN MEDICAL COSTS ISOLATED TO COMMERCIAL SEGMENT - CONF. CALL.ANTHEM CEO SAYS CHALLENGES CO FACES HEADING INTO 2020 ARE "MANAGEABLE" - CONF. CALL.ANTHEM CEO SEES 2020 CORE EPS GROWTH AT LOW END OF 12% TO 15% TARGET GROWTH RATE RELATIVE TO ORIGINAL 2019 GUIDANCE - CONF. CALL.ANTHEM CEO SAYS CONTINUES TO EXPECT NEW PBM INGENIORX WILL PRODUCE TOTAL OPERATING GAIN OF AT LEAST $800 MILLION OR ROUGHLY $2.30 PER SHARE IN 2020 - CONF. CALL.ANTHEM SAYS INCREASE IN 2019 CONSOLIDATED MEDICAL LOSS RATIO IS DUE TO MEDICAID- CONF. CALL.ANTHEM SAYS "VERY BULLISH" FOR 2020 SELLING SEASON FOR MEDICARE - CONF. CALL.ANTHEM CEO SAYS "VERY POSITIVE" ABOUT THE OVERALL MEDICAID ENVIRONMENT BUSINESS GOING FORWARD - CONF. CALL.'}
