{'symbol': 'WU', 'date': '2019-10-23 22:30:00', 'title': 'The Western Union Company Expands Its Global Platform Now to New Partners in Asia', 'text': 'The Western Union Company further expanded its white label offerings to Asia enabling customers of third-party money transfer companies to pay out through Western Union. Customers of Japan’s oldest remittance company KYODAI Remittance, a service of Unidos Co. Ltd., and Korea’s leading fintech company Hanpass, became the latest collaborators to move funds globally through Western Union. Their customers may choose to pay out into billions of bank accounts in more than 100 countries, millions of wallets in a dozen countries or the Western Union® retail Agent network across 200 countries and territories.'}
{'symbol': 'WHR', 'date': '2019-10-23 11:30:00', 'title': 'Whirlpool CFO Says India Continues To Be Very Strong Business With Very Strong Margins', 'text': 'WHIRLPOOL CFO-INDIA CONTINUES TO BE A VERY STRONG BUSINESS WITH VERY STRONG MARGINS-CONF CALL.WHIRLPOOL CEO SAYS THE UNFAVORABLE IMPACT OF PREVIOUSLY ANNOUNCED TARIFFS EXPECTED TO BE OFFSET BY EASING MATERIAL COSTS-CONF CALLL.'}
{'symbol': 'WHR', 'date': '2019-10-23 22:30:00', 'title': 'The ownership group comprising former Whirlpool SA executives and other investors completed the acquisition of Whirlpool South Africa (Proprietary) Limited from Whirlpool Corporation (NYSE:WHR).', 'text': 'The ownership group comprising former Whirlpool SA executives and other investors entered into an agreement to acquire Whirlpool South Africa (Proprietary) Limited from Whirlpool Corporation (NYSE:WHR) for $5 million on June 28, 2019. The purchase price to be paid in cash is subject to customary adjustments at closing. Whirlpool will continue to operate as usual in South Africa until the sale is concluded. The new ownership group will continue to market and distribute their other brands in South Africa and surrounding countries – including the Whirlpool, Indesit, and Ariston brands. Employees (including those at the Isithebe plant) will continue to work with the new company. The transaction will have no effect on service commitments or warranties. The transaction is subject to customary regulatory reviews and approvals. The sale is expected to close during the third quarter of 2019.\nThe ownership group comprising former Whirlpool SA executives and other investors completed the acquisition of Whirlpool South Africa (Proprietary) Limited from Whirlpool Corporation (NYSE:WHR) on October 23, 2019.\n'}
{'symbol': 'WHR', 'date': '2019-10-23 18:30:00', 'title': 'Whirlpool Q3 Sales $5.1 Bln Versus Refinitiv IBES Est. Of $5.13 Bln', 'text': 'ORATION REPORTS STRONG THIRD-QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.97 FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS.Q3 SALES $5.1 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $5.13 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $3.89 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.REAFFIRMS ITS FULL-YEAR CASH FLOW GUIDANCE.FOR FULL-YEAR 2019, COMPANY DECREASED ITS GAAP EARNINGS PER DILUTED SHARE GUIDANCE TO $16.80 TO $17.55.FOR FY 2019, CO HAS REAFFIRMED ITS ONGOING EARNINGS PER DILUTED SHARE GUIDANCE OF $14.75 TO $15.50.WHIRLPOOL - EARNINGS AS A PERCENT OF SALES IN QUARTER, WAS FAVORABLY IMPACTED BY A GAIN ON SALE OF EMBRACO COMPRESSOR BUSINESS OF APPROXIMATELY $511 MILLION.WHIRLPOOL NORTH AMERICA REPORTED THIRD-QUARTER NET SALES OF $3.0 BILLION, COMPARED TO $3.0 BILLION IN SAME PRIOR-YEAR PERIOD.WHIRLPOOL EUROPE, MIDDLE EAST AND AFRICA REPORTED THIRD-QUARTER NET SALES OF $1.1 BILLION, COMPARED TO $1.1 BILLION IN SAME PRIOR-YEAR PERIOD.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $15.27 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}
